ndlord. By passing, I force the Landlord (the next player) to either use a very high card (Ace or 2) to beat the King or allow my teammate to maintain control. I hold a very strong hand with the Rocket, a pair of 2s, and a pair of Aces. The optimal strategy is to wait for the Landlord to play his high cards (like an Ace) and then capture them with my 2s or Rocket, rather than wasting my strength against my partner.\n\nReason: My teammate played a strong card (King). I should not beat it. Passing forces the Landlord to break his hand or use high cards to regain control. If the Landlord plays an Ace, I am well-positioned to beat it with a 2.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
